aarch64 #23 milestone-1: mint host-self and thread-self ports in-guest.

With the host queries served in-guest (0051/0052) the host port is only ever a query destination and a
guarded deallocate, so host_self_trap_impl mints it from the guest port table instead of the RPC.
thread_self_trap_impl likewise mints the thread-self port (per-context cache; single thread per context
for exec-true -- a multi-threaded guest, milestone 6, will need this in TLS, and __thread_self_trap_reset
is provided for the fork child). Deallocate of the minted names is served in-guest.

Verified: exec-true RECV 54 -> 46 (host_self_trap 4 -> 0, thread_self_trap 7 -> 3), rc=0, soak 8/8. The
3 remaining thread_self_trap are the dyld-loader copy (not rebuilt in the buck2 dylib-only swap).
Flag-off unchanged. On top of 0053.

